+    // Prompt-path copy staging pool. The singleton sync_staging pins the
+    // expert-weight copy stream to one copy deep: copy N+1 cannot stage until
+    // copy N's copyBuffer has been consumed by the GPU. Slots break that, but
+    // slots alone are not enough — one submit and one fence wait PER COPY is
+    // ~13,700 round trips per pass, and each costs more in queue latency than
+    // the GPU work it waits for. So copies are staged into slots and submitted
+    // in BATCHES: one submit, one fence, many copyBuffers. Half the slots hold
+    // the batch being read while the GPU drains the previous one.
